      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5dc5b9b25689666d718db510|full_name}: I think that the problem is that the client does everything and the server just says \"ok\" and lets it happen. It shouldn't be that hard to make a couple of checks in the servers. I mean, I only have about three years of experience with coding and my own website already checks if the user has permission to do any action server-side. I can't believe I'm saying this but it has more security than VRChat and it's a one person project. The rule number one of securing your app/game/whatever is never trust the client and always check server-side.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
